# Firebase web config for production builds (`next build` on Vercel, or the Docker build).
# These four values are public by design: Next.js inlines them into the browser bundle, and Firebase
# protects the project with Auth's authorised domains and Firestore rules, not by hiding them.
# Fill them in from Firebase console > Project settings > Your apps > Web app, then commit.
# Left empty, the app builds and serves its public pages and the demo, and sign-in says it isn't configured.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN is the app's own host (e.g. utsav-planner.vercel.app), because
# /__/auth is proxied same-origin to <project>.firebaseapp.com (see README "Deploy").
# Never put secrets here: server-side settings are the host's environment variables (Vercel or Cloud Run).
# A value set in the build environment (or `docker build --build-arg`) overrides this file.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyATctHl6TCxmF8bfVlaXNjN1fWrFMRXPlM
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=utsav-9e004.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=utsav-9e004
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:773838892224:web:88c9fd7e9d7341702c1125
